[[2047,127,0,"<p><a href=\"#/3237719\">1092E22</a></p>"],[264,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the counter-balance shaft drive\nbelt drive pulley (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2014802.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[264,127,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Place the counter-balance shaft drive belt\ndrive pulley back in its housing and secure it tightening the bolts\nto the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COUNTER-ROTATING SHAFT DRIVE PULLEY</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Timing drive pulley side.) 0.8÷1.0</p></td></tr></table></div>"]]